From: TacoRocket
Subject: [PATCH] renderer: native NV12 output with producer storage

Apply after 0001-nv12-direct-output-match.patch on libplacebo v7.360.1.

With ETV_INLINE_NV12=native, libplacebo keeps its own NV12 output and
chroma filter (Mitchell) unchanged, but writes Y during the color pass and
keeps UV in RG16F scratch for the existing chroma passes, instead of
rendering a full-resolution intermediate first. This is the producer-storage
path of TacoRocket/ErsatzTV-ffmpeg PR80 with its padding extension, moved
behind the selector of the base patch.

It assumes the fp16 attachment truncation measured on Intel ANV; Vulkan
does not promise this rounding on other devices. The gate covers 1920x1080
output, full frame or an even-aligned rectangle inside bars. On the
i3-1220P its output is byte-identical to the previous producer-storage
patches over 24 frames of full-frame, pillarbox and letterbox fixtures.

LGPL-2.1-or-later.
